Hmm, let me think about the -m/-M/-n/-N semantics:
- Default (compressing): store name and time ✓ (-N default).
- Default (decompressing): restore neither ✓ (-n default).
- -n: don't store/restore name or time ✓.
- -N: store/restore both ✓.
- -m: don't store/restore the time ✓ (but keep the name).
- -M: store/restore the time ✓.
- The order matters: "-Nm" stores the name but not the time ✓; "-nM" stores the time but not the name ✓.

